# Always expand WA, CSC, and other acronyms (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-28):

> **When referring to WA, CSC, and other acronyms, ALWAYS spell out
> what they mean and their usage.**

## The rule

> **Every acronym in operator-facing chat, commits, docs you author,
> UI strings, OpenAPI, and evidence notes is expanded on first use in
> that artifact: full name, then the acronym, then a short usage
> clause.** Never write bare `WA`, `CSC`, or similar as if the reader
> already knows them.

**Usage clause** means not only "WA = Workstation Assurance" but
"Workstation Assurance (WA) - the endpoint posture scan used on this
workstation role."

After that first expansion in the **same** artifact, later sentences
may use the acronym alone.

## Canonical expansions (US English)

| Acronym | Spell out | Usage (one clause) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| WA | Workstation Assurance | endpoint posture / attest / agent (or agentless admin-channel) checks on a system |
| CSC | Current State Compliance | admin page/ledger of control-oriented findings and rescan, not an Organization Seeking Assessment (OSA) Met stamp |
| PIM | Privileged Identity Management | credential lifecycle / vaulted identities |
| PAM | Privileged Access Management | session Connect/Open, Jump, recording |
| PUM | Privileged User Management | product module; do not invent features |
| IGA | Identity Governance and Administration | roadmap; only when the surface exists |
| CUI | Controlled Unclassified Information | marking / handling scope |
| FCI | Federal Contract Information | marking / handling scope |
| HSM | Hardware Security Module | key custody |
| AIC | Analog Information / product suite name as already used in chrome | do not expand into the marketed toolkit name except Help -> About ([`no-competitor-names-in-website.mdc`](no-competitor-names-in-website.mdc)) |
| PAW | Privileged Access Workstation | hardened seat used for privileged Connect / Open |
| OSA | Organization Seeking Assessment | the customer organization an assessor evaluates; never the product |
| C3PAO | CMMC Third-Party Assessment Organization | assessor who reads binder and operator surfaces |
| IdP | Identity Provider | authentication binding; roster row stays the durable person |
| IAM | Identity and Access Management | local logon, sessions, and role bindings |
| MFA | Multi-Factor Authentication | password plus a second step |
| RBAC | Role-Based Access Control | permission checks on admin and enclave routes |
| VDI | Virtual Desktop Infrastructure | interactive desktop session reached through Connect |
| POA&M | Plan of Action and Milestones | tracked remediation item, not a Met stamp |
| WEL | Windows Event Log | native Windows audit / operational channel |
| MSP | Managed Service Provider | operator who runs the console for a customer |
| OT | Operational Technology | industrial / control-system inventory and access |
| IR | Incident Response | detections, notices, and evidence - not a Met claim |
| DLP | Data Loss Prevention | future file-marking / exfil controls |
| SBOM | Software Bill of Materials | component inventory for a build |
| ATO | Authorization to Operate | agency authorization; not a product SKU claim |
| FedRAMP | Federal Risk and Authorization Management Program | federal authorization program |
| CMVP | Cryptographic Module Validation Program | FIPS module certificate boundary |
| KEK | Key Encryption Key | wraps data keys; lives on HSM or software custody |
| WCAG | Web Content Accessibility Guidelines | Section 508 floor (WCAG 2.0 AA) |
| SIEM | Security Information and Event Management | collector for Windows Event Log and syslog |
| mTLS | mutual Transport Layer Security | client-certificate authentication |
| SPA | Single-Page Application | the admin console embedded in AIC Server |

Cybersecurity Maturity Model Certification (CMMC), National Institute
of Standards and Technology (NIST), and Federal Information Processing
Standards (FIPS) may stay as known authority initialisms **after**
first expansion in a long doc. Same for Access Control family labels
such as AC-16 when already introduced (still pair the short title per
[`control-lists-short-title.mdc`](control-lists-short-title.mdc)).

If you introduce an acronym that is not in this table, expand it the
same way: full name, acronym, usage clause. Do not invent product
features while explaining Privileged User Management (PUM) or Identity
Governance and Administration (IGA).

## Where it applies

Chat replies, commit subjects and bodies, docs you author, UI strings
and locale catalogs, OpenAPI descriptions, evidence notes, and
operator-visible API error text.

**Not this rule:** historical path / crate / table / route identifiers
(`pim-offline-server`, `offline_*`, `/api/offline/*`); code tokens
(`wa_agent`, `csc_findings`); Cursor rule **filenames**. Comments,
UI copy, and docs that sit next to those identifiers still expand.

## Required shape

```text
Workstation Assurance (WA) - the endpoint posture and attest checks
on this system
```

Authority long-doc first use:

```text
Cybersecurity Maturity Model Certification (CMMC)
```

## Forbidden constructs

- Bare `WA`, `CSC`, or a similar product acronym in a user-facing
  reply, commit, UI string, OpenAPI text, or evidence note with no
  prior expansion in that artifact
- Expansion without a usage clause ("WA = Workstation Assurance"
  and nothing about what it does)
- Expanding Analog Information / product suite (AIC) into the
  marketed toolkit name except Help -> About
- Treating Current State Compliance (CSC) copy as an Organization
  Seeking Assessment (OSA) Met stamp
  ([`compliance-claims-honesty.mdc`](compliance-claims-honesty.mdc))
- Competitor brand names in examples
  ([`no-competitor-names-in-website.mdc`](no-competitor-names-in-website.mdc))
- Lab hostnames or agent thinking inside the usage clause
  ([`no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc`](no-lab-config-in-operator-ui.mdc))

## Worked example

**Violation** (chat, UI helper, or evidence note):

```text
WA is down. Open CSC and rescan.
```

**Fix** (first use in that artifact):

```text
Workstation Assurance (WA) - the endpoint posture and attest checks
on this system - is down. Open Current State Compliance (CSC) - the
admin ledger of control-oriented findings and rescan, not an
Organization Seeking Assessment (OSA) Met stamp - and run Rescan.
```

Later sentences in the same artifact may say WA and CSC.

## Agent duty

1. Expand on first use in every artifact you write.
2. Add a new row to this table when a product acronym becomes
   common; keep US English and ASCII hyphens.
3. Mirror this file to
   `core-assets/.cursor/rules/expand-acronyms-on-first-use.mdc`
   in the same change set
   ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)) - the workspace
   `.cursor` directory is not a git root.

